@Graphics editing
This menu can be used to edit the graphics for the game. If the graphics
are not defined then the default graphics (PC characters and colours) will
be used, so using this menu is not mandatory for making a game world.

!chr;Font (simple)
!fnt;Font (advanced)
!pal;Palette

!glo;Global options

:chr;Font (simple)
This is for making simple 8x14 full fonts with 256 characters. These fonts
cannot include animations, character code mapping, etc, and cannot be
partial fonts, and are also not compressed.

:fnt;Font (advanced)
Not implemented yet.

:pal;Palette
Defines a palette.

:glo;Global options
The graphics global options contains the following settings:

þ 40 columns: If selected, then the display during the game will use 40
columns; if not selected, then it will use 80 columns. Some built-in menus
will always use 80 columns regardless of this. Note that if it is set to 40
columns then only the first 40 columns of the screen are used and the other
40 columns will not be displayed.

þ Mandatory font/palettes: If selected, then it means that this world file
requires these fonts/palettes for the game to work properly. Super ZZ Zero
will refuse to run the world if you try to run it on a computer that is not
capable of using these features.

þ Recommended font/palettes: If selected, then it is recommended to use the
custom fonts/palettes included in the world file; it will not work as well,
but is still playable, if they are not used. A warning message will be
displayed if you try to run it on a computer that cannot use custom fonts.

þ Main font: The name of the main font to use. Leave it blank to use the
built-in PC font.

þ Main palette: The name of the main palette to use. Leave it blank to use
the built-in PC colours.

